          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The term
            %em tensor network
            has become popular in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            for essentially what in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
            is known as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Penrose+notation"} Penrose notation
            and in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            is referred to as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagrams"} string diagrams
            (see
            %a{:href => "#BCJ10"} BCJ 10
            for a bilingual account).
          %p
            The term rose to prominence in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            partly with discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+quantum+mechanics+in+terms+of+dagger-compact+categories"} finite quantum mechanics in terms of dagger-compact categories
            but mainly via its use for representing highly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entangled+states"} entangled states
            in the discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbative effects
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
            (
            %a{:href => "#Swingle09"}> Swingle 09
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Swingle13"} Swingle 13
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
            and thus to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
          %p
            In this context, a
            %em tensor network
            is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concept+with+an+attitude"} with an attitude
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
              (typically regarded in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite-dimensional vector spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
              etc.), but with:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                of all its external
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                regarded as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states"} space of states
                of a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum system
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} element
                in that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                defined by the string diagram regarded as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/state"} state
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+function"}> wave function
                ) of that quantum system.
          %p
            For instance, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+Lie+algebra"} metric Lie algebra
            (with
            = succeed "-notation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "metric+Lie+algebra#Definition"} there
            = succeed "-power" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual vector space
            regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product"} inner product
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+tensor+network+state"} tree tensor network state
            is the following:
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/TensorNetworkStateFromMetricLieAlgebra.jpg", :width => "300"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
            arising this way are generically highly
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entangled+state"} entangled
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            there are in the corresponding tensor network.
          %p
            The following is an example of what is called a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+product+state"} matrix product state
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/MatrixProductStateFromMetricLieAlgebra.jpg", :width => "300"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree+tensor+network+states"} tree tensor network states
            in the form of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruhat-Tits+trees"} Bruhat-Tits trees
            play a special role in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} AdS/CFT correspondence
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a kind of
                = succeed "-approximation" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QFT"} lattice QFT
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CFT"} CFT
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            %li
              %p
                as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+geometry"} p-adic geometric
                incarnation of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
                in the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+AdS%2FCFT+correspondence"} p-adic AdS/CFT correspondence
            %li
              %p
                as a reflection of actual
                = succeed "-site" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystal"} crystal
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+in+solid+state+physics"} AdS/CFT in solid state physics
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BruhatTitsTreeTensorNetworkStateFromMetricLie.jpg", :width => "300"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Cohomotopy+implies+intersecting+brane+observables"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
          %p
            (As in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "p-adic+AdS/CFT+correspondence#HMSS16"} HMSS 16
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "p-adic+AdS/CFT+correspondence#HLM19"} HLM 19
            = succeed "?)" do
              %a{:href => "p-adic+AdS/CFT+correspondence#HMPS18"} HMPS 18
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network+states"} tensor network states
            dual to tesselations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+space"} hyperbolic space
            and made from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+tensors"} perfect tensors
            one finds that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            of the tensor subspace associated with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            becomes proportional, for large number of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+space"} hyperbolic
            bulk boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/length"} length
            of the segment of the tree network that ends on this interval, according to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ryu-Takayanagi+formula"} Ryu-Takayanagi formula
            (
            %a{:href => "#PYHP15"}> PYHP 15, Theorem 2
            ). Hence one speaks of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ForHolographicEntanglementEntropy"} below
          %p
            General tensor network states are mixtures of the above examples. For instance in … is the suggestion that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BTZ+black+holes"} BTZ black holes
            are encoded by networks that look like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruhat-Tits+trees"} Bruhat-Tits trees
            towards the boundaries and like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+product+states"} matrix product states
            towards the interior:
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/BTZTensorNetworksStateFromLieAlgebra.jpg", :width => "350"}/
          %p
            (As in
            = succeed ".)" do
